The things worth preserving are the ones that progressively remove our assumptions while strengthening observation. I’d combine them into a final blueprint something like this:

WORLDHEART — Emergent Computational Petri Dish

Final Concept Blueprint

Core hypothesis

Instead of programming artificial agents and asking whether they can behave intelligently, construct a computational environment in which persistent organization, representation, learning, agency and potentially cognition-like structures are possible outcomes rather than predefined features.

Consciousness is neither implemented nor assumed.

If something interesting emerges, preserve it first and investigate it second.

